+# Pickup reminders
+
+For whoever changes how members are reminded of a pickup, or proposes moving reminders from SMS to email to save its
+cost. The day before a pickup, larder sends the member a reminder by SMS. Reminders went by email from April to June
+2025 to save the SMS cost, and missed pickups more than doubled, so they went back to SMS.
+
+## Reminder
+
+The day before the pickup slot, `remind` in `larder/reminders.py` sends the member "Your pantry order is ready for
+pickup" with the slot. `CHANNEL` in the same file picks the channel: `sms` sends to the member's phone, any other
+value to their email.
+
+## Why SMS, not email
+
+SMS costs about 40 euros a month; email is free, and volunteers have proposed switching more than once, the latest in
+issue 52, where three people had asked within the year.
+
+From April to June 2025 reminders went by email. The email provider's report showed 34% of reminder emails never
+opened, and missed pickups rose from 6% of pantry orders to 13%. A missed pickup is a bag packed for nothing, and the
+fresh food in it is thrown away at closing time. Many members share one phone across the family and never check
+email; an SMS they see.
+
+Reminders went back to SMS on July 1, 2025, and missed pickups were back to 6% by August. In issue 52 the
+maintainer kept SMS and closed the proposal.
